.env*
*.sqlite
*node_modules

# Build artifacts. Odin names these per platform, so the same `-build-mode` produces a different
# extension on each one and both halves of the list are needed for a repo that CI builds on three
# platforms. Every recipe in the justfile passes `-out:target/...`, so in practice these only catch
# an ad-hoc `odin build .` run from the repository root.
#
#   build mode      Windows     Linux       macOS
#   (default)       .exe        <dirname>   <dirname>
#   obj             .obj        .o          .o
#   shared          .dll        .so         .dylib
#   static          .lib        .a          .a
#   llvm-ir         .ll         .ll         .ll
#   -debug          .pdb        (in binary) .dSYM bundle
#
# The default executable has no extension on Linux and macOS - it takes the name of the package
# directory - so no pattern can catch it. The skeleton sidesteps this by naming its output
# `main.exe` on every platform (see `main_name` in the justfile); a bare `odin build .` is the one
# case that will show up in `git status`.
*.exe
*.obj
*.dll
*.lib
*.exp
*.ilk
*.pdb
*.o
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.a
*.dSYM/
*.bc
*.ll

# Crash dumps. Worth having in a skeleton that ships sanitizer recipes and a segfault handler.
# Deliberately not a bare `core` - that would swallow a package directory of that name.
core.[0-9]*
vgcore.*

# profile data
*.spall

# Editor and debugger state
*.sublime-workspace
*.suo
*.rdbg

# Machine-specific absolute collection path; regenerate with `just ols-config` after cloning.
ols.json

# OS file-manager droppings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Our project outputs artifacts to target/**. A build dir is another common custom directory for artifacts.
build
target

# The Sciter engine is **fetched, not committed**, on every platform - so the build-artifact patterns
# above (*.so, *.dll, *.dylib) already cover it and there is deliberately no negation here. The three
# binaries are 90 MB between them and a binary does not delta-compress, so every engine bump would have
# added ~40 MB to history permanently. `just fetch-engine` downloads the pinned file and verifies it
# against the per-platform SHA-256 in external/sciter/VENDORED.md; `ensure-engine` runs before every
# recipe that builds or runs anything, so a fresh clone needs no step anyone has to remember.
#
# docs/UPGRADING.md is the decision and the arithmetic behind it. If a platform's engine ever goes back
# into the tree, it needs a `!lib/...` negation here - the patterns above are what would silently
# swallow it, which is the bug this comment used to exist to prevent.
lib/linux/x64/libsciter.so
lib/windows/x64/sciter.dll
lib/macosx/libsciter.dylib

# Bytecode from the justfile's `[script]` recipes, which import .github/scripts/justlib.py.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# CodeGraph's local index. Machine-local and regenerable; nothing here should be shared.
.codegraph/
.claude

